## TUI terminal ownership, configurable hotkeys, and Groq rate controls — 2026-11-15

- Added a pausable terminal input reader that acknowledges pauses before child-process launch and reads at most one byte per call, preventing background input consumption and buffered read-ahead into the editor or shell.
- External editors and shells receive foreground process-group ownership. Agy restores its foreground group, raw mode, bracketed paste, enhanced keyboard, and mouse policy on return.
- Model streaming output and UI events are buffered while a child owns the terminal, then flushed/replayed after return. Ctrl+O opens an interactive `$SHELL` even while an LLM request runs; the request context is not cancelled. Ctrl+G remains the prompt editor. Alt+O toggles tool trajectory.
- Ctrl+M is normalized to Enter in enhanced keyboard protocols. Ctrl+J remains newline. IEXTEN is disabled in raw mode so Ctrl+W is handled by Agy rather than the terminal line discipline.
- The model picker Tab key applies the highlighted model in both scrollback and full-screen modes.
- settings.json exposes validated action-to-key mappings; /keybindings displays active assignments. Conflicting bindings are rejected and empty values unbind actions.
- Groq has shared RPM/TPM limiting, configurable output-token cap and 429 retries, and Retry-After/reset-hint parsing. Groq tool requests explicitly use `tool_choice: auto`; GPT-OSS disables parallel tool calls.
- Verified Groq's local function-call protocol with request-body tests: function definitions are sent with `tool_choice: auto`, assistant function calls are followed by tool-role messages carrying the matching `tool_call_id`, and GPT-OSS requests disable parallel calls.
- Added a mocked Groq 429 test using `X-RateLimit-Reset-Tokens`; Agy waits for the reset window and succeeds on the next request. Retry-delay tests cover Retry-After, token-reset duration, and the human-readable ITPM retry phrase.
- Added hotkey defaults, Ctrl+M alias, collision detection, remap/unbind and JSON round-trip tests. Input-reader tests verify child-shell keystrokes are not consumed while Agy's reader is paused.
- Work CI run #1917 (`43679378944`) passed Bash checks, gofmt, `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, Linux amd64 build and artifact upload.
- Remaining: manually verify terminal handoff in an interactive xterm/terminal emulator and adjust any emulator-specific foreground-process behavior reported by real use. No release or main merge requested.

- Tool availability is role- and permission-scoped before the request reaches Groq. Built-in researcher/reviewer/planner roles are read-only and can receive file listing/read/search and web tools, but not shell/write/edit tools. The no-tools role intentionally receives no function tools. Use the default/coder role and an appropriate global permission mode for workspace operations. A claim that only web search is available should be checked against the active `/agent` role and `/config` permissions; a subsequent ITPM 429 is a separate quota failure.
